zl1: the UT camera app starts, and the port's own preload was breaking EGL -- 2026-09-23
=====================================================================================

One boot (uptime ~42,900 s -> the device dropped to EDL, see the last section), no reboot by us, no
partition write. Everything below is what the device printed during the session; the raw files are
on the device under /userdata/zl1-camera/ (app-dbg, app-nons, app-way, app-run1, app-run2, egl-*,
strace-egl.log, probe-*.strace).


THE FAILURE, AS FIRST SEEN
==========================
Running the click package's binary from the host, with the running shell's own environment (the
session env, /proc/<shell pid>/environ) and inside the container's PID namespace:

  ASSERT: "eglInitialize(mEglDisplay, nullptr, nullptr) == EGL_TRUE" in file
          ../../../src/ubuntumirclient/qmirclientintegration.cpp, line 150
  crash-dump: caught signal 6 -- /proc/self/maps follows, then a backtrace of this thread

The maps of that crash had libEGL_mesa.so.0.0.0 and NO libEGL_libhybris.so.0.0.0, and the stderr had
four X11 lines that do not belong in a Mir client's output at all:

  Authorization required, but no authorization protocol specified


THE SAME APP, AS A WAYLAND CLIENT: NOT A PATH QUIETLY TAKEN
===========================================================
ZL1_SET_QT_QPA_PLATFORM=wayland:

  qt.qpa.plugin: Could not find the Qt platform plugin "wayland" in ""
  Available platform plugins are: eglfs, linuxfb, minimal, minimalegl, offscreen, mir1server,
                                   ubuntumirclient, vnc, xcb.

There is no wayland QPA plugin. The only usable one for a UT app here is ubuntumirclient, which is
what the app was already using.


WHO BREAKS, MEASURED RATHER THAN ASSUMED (strace -f -e trace=openat)
====================================================================
The app, without the port's cfi-shadow preload:

  openat("/usr/share/glvnd/egl_vendor.d/10_libhybris.json")  = 8
  openat("/lib/aarch64-linux-gnu/libEGL_libhybris.so.0")     = 8
  openat("/usr/share/glvnd/egl_vendor.d/50_mesa.json")       = 8
  openat("/lib/aarch64-linux-gnu/libEGL_mesa.so.0")          = 8
  openat("/dev/dri", O_DIRECTORY)                            = -1 ENOENT
  --- SIGABRT ---

-- libhybris' EGL is a glvnd vendor ICD, and that is all it is:

  $ readelf -d libEGL_libhybris.so.0.0.0     (pulled to the host and read there)
     NEEDED libhybris-common.so.1, libstdc++.so.6, libc.so.6, libgcc_s.so.1
     SONAME libEGL_libhybris.so.0
  $ nm -D --defined-only libEGL_libhybris.so.0.0.0 | grep egl
     00000000000067d4 T __egl_Main            <- the only egl* symbol; no eglGetDisplay
  $ strings -a | grep eglplatform
     %s/eglplatform_%s.so
     /usr/lib/aarch64-linux-gnu/libhybris/

-- so it reads EGL_PLATFORM and dlopens its platform module from a directory that contains:

  eglplatform_fbdev.so  eglplatform_hwcomposer.so  eglplatform_null.so  eglplatform_wayland.so

  (no mir module: a Mir client cannot be served by a platform module this build does not have)

-- and the working shell does not use glvnd for any of this. It has mapped:

  /android/system/lib64/libEGL.so, /android/vendor/lib64/egl/libEGL_adreno.so,
  /usr/lib/aarch64-linux-gnu/libEGL_libhybris.so.0.0.0,
  /usr/lib/aarch64-linux-gnu/libhybris/eglplatform_null.so,
  /usr/lib/aarch64-linux-gnu/mir1/client-platform/android2.so.5,
  /usr/lib/aarch64-linux-gnu/mir1/server-platform/graphics-android2.so.16

  i.e. Mir's own platform plugins dlopen libhybris' EGL themselves; the Qt client's EGL goes
  through glvnd (libEGL.so.1.1.0, which is a dispatcher: it has no eglGetDisplay implementation of
  its own, only the vendor list).


