  cfi-shadow-init[33976] no android_dlopen/android_dlsym after this object -- not priming
  Authorization required, but no authorization protocol specified     (x12)
  libEGL.so.1                eglGetDisplay(EGL_DEFAULT_DISPLAY) = 0x33446c90
                             eglInitialize = 0 (0.0)

And the same difference in the strace of the probe:

  plain: ... libEGL_libhybris.so.0 -> libhybris-common.so.1 -> libEGL.so.1 -> libhybris/linker/o.so
         -> /android/system/lib64/libEGL.so = 3 -> /vendor/lib64/egl/libEGL_adreno.so = 6
         -> /usr/lib/aarch64-linux-gnu/libhybris//eglplatform_null.so = 6   <- platform module
  cfi:   ... libEGL_libhybris.so.0 -> libhybris-common.so.1 -> libEGL.so.1 -> libhybris/linker/o.so
         -> libEGL_mesa.so.0 = 3 -> ... (no android EGL, no eglplatform_*.so at all)


THE BUG (scripts/cfi-shadow/cfi-shadow-init.c)
==============================================
prime() resolved its forwarding target with dlsym(RTLD_NEXT, "android_dlopen"). RTLD_NEXT searches
the objects *after* this one in the *global* scope, and libhybris-common.so.1 can arrive inside the
local scope of a library glvnd dlopens (libEGL_libhybris.so.0 is dlopened by libEGL.so.1 in every Qt
process), which RTLD_NEXT cannot see. It then returned early, leaving real_dlopen NULL -- and because
android_dlopen() forwards through real_dlopen, the shim answered NULL to *every* hybris dlopen in the
process. state was set to 2 (primed) regardless, so the failure was cached for the process's life.

  cfi-shadow log, the two populations (append-only, per pid):
    90 x  "shadow at 0x..."                                          <- primed (test_camera runs)
    "no android_dlopen/android_dlsym after this object -- not priming" <- the camera app and every
                                                                          probe run of 2026-09-23

For libcamera this was harmless in the other direction: test_camera has libcamera.so.1 as a
DT_NEEDED, so libhybris-common was in the global scope before the first call and priming worked.
The camera app loads libcamera later (through libcamera_compat_layer), and by then the shim had
already poisoned the process.


THE FIX
=======
resolve_real(): try RTLD_NEXT first (unchanged behaviour where it worked), then fall back to
dlopen("libhybris-common.so.1", RTLD_NOW | RTLD_GLOBAL) and take the two symbols from that handle,
logging which route was needed. prime() now returns whether it primed, and android_dlopen() stores 0
back into state when it did not, so a "not yet" is retried instead of being cached as "never".

  $ scripts/cfi-shadow/build.sh
      sha256 1b66341170fe7188b2e87f52cbde568432db99584c0b468fed52907097219056
      (previous: bec52da782a00bbbbcbdf51cb1069ce61aacaf978b46eb33005afb34dc3587be, kept on the
       device as libcfi-shadow-init.so.orig-20260923)
      DT_NEEDED still empty; dlopen added to the undefined list (resolves from libc.so.6)

After it, the same probe with cfi-shadow preloaded:

  cfi-shadow-init[34061] resolved android_dlopen via dlopen("libhybris-common.so.1") -- RTLD_NEXT
                         could not see it (libhybris-common is not in the global scope)
  cfi-shadow-init[34061] shadow at 0x71bba57000, filling the first 8388608 bytes ...
  libEGL.so.1                eglGetDisplay(EGL_DEFAULT_DISPLAY) = 0x1
                             eglInitialize = 1 (1.4)
                             vendor = Android
                             version = 1.4 Android META-EGL


