As root (without ZL1_AS_UID), the same run gets as far as "Added camera 0/1" and then dies:

  QStandardPaths: runtime directory '/run/user/32011' is not owned by UID 0 ...
  ** (process:34068): ERROR **: Error connecting to unix:path=/run/user/32011/bus: The connection
  is closed
  exit=133 (SIGTRAP)

i.e. the session bus rejects a peer whose uid is not 32011, which is why the run has to drop to the
session's own user after reading its environment.


DEVICE STATE AND HOW THIS SESSION ENDED
=======================================
SSH stopped answering at host kernel time 2200800.5; the host's own kernel log shows the transition
on the port the zl1 has always been on (3-3, the RNDIS gadget):

  [2195387.8] rndis_host 3-3:1.0 usb0: unregister 'rndis_host' usb-0000:00:14.0-3, RNDIS device
  [2195388.9] rndis_host 3-3:1.0 usb0: register 'rndis_host' at usb-0000:00:14.0-3, ..., 52:d0:92:1c:83:b6
  [2195607.8] rndis_host 3-3:1.0 usb0: unregister 'rndis_host' usb-0000:00:14.0-3, RNDIS device
  [2195609.9] rndis_host 3-3:1.0 usb0: register 'rndis_host' at usb-0000:00:14.0-3, ..., 86:e0:d0:fb:61:33
  [2200800.5] usb 3-3: USB disconnect, device number 114
  [2200802.2] usb 3-3: New USB device found, idVendor=05c6, idProduct=9008, bcdDevice= 0.00
              idVendor=05c6 idProduct=9008, Product: QUSB__BULK, SerialNumber=0
  [2200802.2] qcserial 3-3:1.0: Qualcomm USB modem converter now attached to ttyUSB2

05c6:9008 with product QUSB__BULK is Qualcomm EDL (the emergency download loader), now steady on
3-3 for 80+ s with no serial number. Nothing in this session wrote to a partition, the boot image,
or a modem/radio partition, and no EDL/QDL/QFIL tool was run. Which side caused the transition is
not established: the camera app had been running (as the session user, with the hybris camera path
open in the container) a couple of minutes earlier, the device had re-enumerated its RNDIS gadget
twice before that, and on this SoC the end of certain fault paths is EDL -- docs/ubuntu-touch/49
section 5 recorded the same presentation (05c6:9008 on port 3-3) after an unrelated driver unbind,
and it was recovered with a long press on power, not with any tool. It is recorded here as an
unexplained transition, not as a diagnosis.

The device needs a physical reset (long press on power) to leave EDL; there is no software path to
it that does not go through the QDL loader, which the port's own ground rules forbid. No EDL tool was
run from this side.


WHAT THIS SESSION DID NOT ESTABLISH
===================================
- Whether the app's window reaches the screen: the display was off (ActiveOutputs (ii) 0 0) for
  every run in this session and the compositor's CPU was never sampled with the app alive, so the
  doc 68/77 criterion (2 ticks/s with no client vs 20-26 with a preview, display ON) was not applied.
- Whether the preview works in the app: the camera was enumerated ("Added camera 0/1") but no frame
  was looked for.
- Why "/system/lib64/libui_compat_layer.so" is asked for by absolute path: /android/system is a
  read-only ext4 mount (/dev/loop1), so the shim in /userdata/zl1-hybris/lib cannot be reached by
  that name, and the file was not placed there. The message is non-fatal in the run above.
- Why the media-hub session fails ("No such object path '/com/lomiri/MediaHub/Service/sessions/0'").
